## BLUF
PR #1007 raises parts A and B at head `b28ed490ada70df2056763f4512c98443285a694`, not yet merged. `system-status.ts` no longer resolves service or portal URLs to the decommissioned `secuura-staging-*` / `ashypond…westeurope` estate under `NODE_ENV=staging`. **This ticket stays open.**

## Recommendation
No action needed on the PR. Remaining on this ticket:
- (1) the 17 call sites still pass `'secuura-staging-<svc>'` as the now-unused third argument;
- (2) the `/system/status` remediation hint at `routes/system-status.ts:527` still reads `az containerapp revision restart --name secuura-staging-${service.name} --resource-group secuura-staging-rg`;
- (3) item 2 from 2026-09-12: portals probed on `:80` while nginx serves `:8080` (Part B's default stays `:80`);
- (4) item 3: the headline ignores red panels.

## Detail
- PR: https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/1007 (branch `feature/ks-864-ornith-dead-estate-pointers`, base develop `40fe4db69`).
- Authored by the local model (Ornith) from a Wednesday-written brief; source-read by Wednesday; re-run by seat A at `b28ed490ada70df2056763f4512c98443285a694`.
- Measured `grep -c 'ashypond\|westeurope\|secuura-staging-' system-status.ts`: 22 on develop, **18** after A+B. That is the 17 call-site arguments plus the `:527` hint; the brief expected 17.
- Red before green:
  - both files on the untouched product: 4 of 6 red;
  - after Part A: A green, B still red;
  - after A+B: 6/6.
- Tampers:
  - A's staging branch restored → A's two 🔴 cells;
  - the issuer ternary restored → B's two 🔴 cells;
  - the env var ignored → both controls.
- api-gateway 44 files / 388 tests pass (baseline 42 / 382). `tsc` rc 0.
